D2=*;
D3=*;
D4=*;
D5=*;
/COVARIANCES
/PRINT
EIS;
FIT=ALL;
TABLE=EQUATION;
/END

And this is my model specification in R:

model =
'
       ### Latent variables

        F1 =~ V1 + V2 + V3 + V4
        F2 =~ V5 + V6 + V7
        F3 =~ V8 + V9 + V10 + V11
        F4 =~ V12 + V13 + V14 + V15
        F5 =~ V16 + V17 + V18 + V19
        F6 =~ V20

        ### Structural equation

        F5 ~ F1
        F2 ~ F6 + F5 + F1
        F3 ~ F6 + F5 + F1
        F4 ~ F6 + F5 + F1

        ### Var

        F1 ~~ 1*F1
        F6 ~~ 1*F6
'

fit = sem(model, data = data, estimator = "MLR")
summary(fit)

I do not understand the mistake ...
Thanks to all for your invaluable help :)

Why do you say there is a mistake? Is there an error message? Different results?

